## 🎯 Daily Challenge

Consider the following tables:

**Employee(EmpID, Name, DeptID, Salary)**

| EmpID | Name  | DeptID | Salary |
| ----: | ----- | -----: | -----: |
|     1 | Asha  |     10 |  50000 |
|     2 | Ravi  |     20 |  60000 |
|     3 | Neha  |     10 |  70000 |
|     4 | Karan |     30 |  55000 |

**Department(DeptID, DeptName)**

| DeptID | DeptName |
| -----: | -------- |
|     10 | CSE      |
|     20 | ECE      |
|     30 | ME       |

Write SQL queries to:

1. Display the names of employees working in the **CSE** department.
2. Find the **average salary** of each department.
3. Display departments having an average salary **greater than 55,000**.
4. Find employees whose salary is **greater than the overall average salary**.

These are classic GATE and placement interview SQL questions.
